  "A4_r_eff_collision": {
    "E-27.6_T6": "r_eff = exp(-sum p ln p) of the symmetrized 32x32 CROSS-DOCUMENT cosine matrix K^F (n=32 docs). K^F is built from Jb = p_i(J_i - sum_j p_j J_j) = P(p_t)J (exp27_6_isolation.py:72-73) => slice CANONICAL, not raw, and it is NOT the ESG (JJ^T) spectrum over K=128 modes (self-correction, review v2 N3): it is a document-similarity spectrum, and paper.md 2.3 declares cross-sample pools invalid (C_b ~ 0.003-0.05), so it is not an ESG dimension estimate. Observed range 24.4-31.6 (max = n_docs = 32)",
    "E-39a": "r_eff(tau) = threshold participation ratio of U_obs (hidden covariance): body r_eff(0.05)=178, per-doc 31 — observation-space object",
    "collision": "two different objects share the name r_eff (neither is an ESG spectrum: T6 is doc-similarity, E-39a is observation space); the '98-99% vs r_eff=24-31' contradiction was ALREADY dissolved by E-39-suppl (norm vs energy); tier-0 must always name the subscript: r_eff^ESG vs r_eff^U(tau)",
    "open": "закрыто в этом же прогоне: p_slice спектров E-27.5/27.6 = p_t (POS=0 основной срез, POS=32 T5) — «p0» в имени S64K64p0 это индекс позиции, не фиксированная p0 (код-аудит, E40_0_gate); НОВОЕ следствие: срез T6 = canonical (P(p_t)J), т.е. ответ на §3.1(b) изменён на canonical; lineage C_F/C_top16 = exp31 raw => пересчёт в E-40.2"
  },
